+- On 2026-10-01 the customer replaced three old locale concept PNGs with the single [current switcher render](design/references/locale-switcher/README.md) (CHG-0046). The closed control is now bare flag + uppercase two-letter code + chevron, fixed at one x/y header position while scrolling; it changes to light code only over source-mapped dark artwork. The existing light translucent 11-language dropdown and its selection logic remain. The 2026-09-30 [implementation report](docs/locale-switcher-implementation-2026-09-30.md) describes a historical capsule/scrolled position; the new render supersedes that portion only. The original product art and copy are still governed by the main references. Platform emoji appearance varies. An unrelated missing favicon remains open as CHG-0035.
+- [CHG-0036](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0036) remains the current dropdown design: light `rgb(250 247 242 / .45)` panel, dark names, fine gold rim, 112px width, no checkmark and highlighted current row. The earlier graphite panel and [CHG-0037](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0037) capsule alignment/scrolled relocation are historical closed-control states, superseded by CHG-0046. The old [follow-up report](docs/locale-switcher-follow-up-2026-10-01.md) retains its original dropdown evidence. Separate favicon CHG-0035 and absolute scroll restoration CHG-0038 remain open.
 - On 2026-10-01, the user's active `:3020` production preview was found serving an older CSS build despite the verified CHG-0036/0037 source. It was rebuilt and restarted; fresh live screenshots show the translucent gold-rimmed menu and desktop header centers within 1.5 CSS px. Addressed preview tests passed (3 applicable, 3 profile skips). The repeated report and root cause are appended to CHG-0036/0037; see the preview freshness lesson in [LESSONS.md](LESSONS.md). The `:3020` server remains the current preview; a later source change requires another build and restart.

